From 707a3bee7b61dd31648f750341c29f3b8677efa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:46:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-sync): retire audited fenced phantom run uploads
 [daveey]

The live-claim restoration path deletes/tombstones phantom task_runs as well
as lifecycle events, but rejection retirement only recognized task_events.
A never-stored synthesized run therefore left permanent rejected-outbox drift.

Extend the existing conservative phantom rule to task_runs, preserving exact
rejection audit, primary mode, absent local row, exact tombstone, no pending
work, never_existed/floor=0 evidence and transactional provenance revalidation.
No historical write is replayed; no lease, tombstone or audit is changed.

Proof: normal-round regression RED on base, GREEN with fix; 986 tests in nine
sync/rejection/reserved-key/dependency consumer suites passed. Expanded every
predicate/race/mutation control to both tables; repaired the table-veto control
to keep adjacent audit/tombstone conditions valid. scripts/check: 21 checks ok.
Read-only live replay over hub live boards and replicas: exactly two changed
verdicts, both the diagnosed phantom run UIDs, with authenticated never_existed
floor=0 evidence. Settled baseline head 3998143 had no other row differences.
